} else {
  qaOnlyAnswer = [running block]
}
```

The condition is `qaJob.result && qaIsTerminal`. If the job is terminal but result is null (race between status flip and result attachment), it falls into the running branch → renders "RUNNING (completed, 100%)". Same bug as Defect 1.

Let me fix this. But first, let me also check — the QA runtime actually RAN on the server (the worker job completed), so the fix is just the answer rendering. Let me fix the QA-only block to handle terminal-without-result like I did for read-only inspection.

Actually, let me also check whether the worker actually ran the QA tests. The job status is completed/COMPLETED which means the worker's QA branch executed. But the answer shows placeholder text because of the rendering bug. Let me fix this.

Let me fix the QA-only answer rendering to handle terminal-without-result, then re-test. I also need to run live cert test 1 (code-change).

